Answer the question that is posed. What does this string routine return?
String s = "dydyd";
int i = 0, j = s.length() - 1;
while (i < j) { if (s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)) return false; i++; j--; }
return true;

Study the setup and answer it. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {3, 7, 11, 12, 16, 20, 21, 22};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 33) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 33) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Compute the result for this case. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(10);
Node b = new Node(35);
Node c = new Node(15);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

